<h1>About batch.recipes</h1>
<p><strong>A free site that turns a recipe into a batch plan: grocery list, cook order, fridge and freezer plan.</strong> Add a screenshot or paste the text, pick how many meals, and it does the rest.</p>
<p>For meal preppers who save recipes from TikTok and Reels.</p>

<h2>What you get</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The recipe, scaled</strong> to the meals you pick, in cups, ounces and pounds.</li>
<li><strong>A grocery list in store order.</strong> Tick it off as you shop, or send it to Reminders, Notes or Keep.</li>
<li><strong>A cook order</strong>, one step at a time, with the screen kept on.</li>
<li><strong>Where it all goes</strong>: freezer, fridge, and what to add fresh.</li>
<li><strong>Freezer labels</strong> for Avery 5160 sheets, or as an image.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<h3>Is it free?</h3>
<p>Yes. No account. Store links and ads keep it free.</p>
<h3>Where are my recipes saved?</h3>
<p>On your phone or computer. Back them up to a file to move them.</p>
<h3>What happens to my screenshots?</h3>
<p>An AI reader reads them and doesn't keep them. If it can't, they're read on your device instead. More in <a href="privacy">Privacy</a>.</p>
<h3>Is there an app?</h3>
<p>It runs in the browser. Add it to your Home Screen to use it as an app.</p>

<p><a href="guides">All guides</a>: how much rice, how big a pot, how to double a recipe.</p>

<p>Made by Michael Begley.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Ideas, bugs or questions: open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/michaelbegley/batch.day/issues" rel="noopener">github.com/michaelbegley/batch.day</a>.</p>
